  "body": "Source: https://github.com/w3c/hr-time/pull/14 /cc @bzbarsky\n\n> So we do want something like the \"current document\" concept; this spec gets that right. And we want it defined in HTML, because other specs need it too (e.g. https://w3c.github.io/requestidlecallback/ wants the same concept; it's currently incorrectly using \"active document\"). That will allow us to have a clear definition of the \"current document\" of a Window, since HTML can just define in the processing model when it gets updated.\n> \n> Again, my issue is with the use of the term \"document\" to refer to something other than a Document object in this spec, and the lack of clarity about what that something is.\n",
